# Timetable imported from a local railpull crawl. Real NTES data: kept out of the
# repository because railpull's README warns that redistributing it may run against
# the operator's terms of use. Re-crawl rather than passing it on.
# data/timetable_danapur.imported.csv is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is a 40 KB derived extract -- 543 services over one division, reduced to the ten
# columns this model needs -- not a copy of any source book. Committing it is what makes
# a clone plan against published times rather than the approximate ones, which is the
# difference between demonstrating the idea and demonstrating the system. Its own header
# carries the attribution and the regenerate-rather-than-copy note.
#
# The datasets it derives from stay out: they are 116 MB and their licences are not this
# repository's to grant.

# NOTE on web/public/plan.json (deliberately NOT ignored).
#
# It is ~2.7 MB and rewritten on every pipeline run, so committing it does add a blob to
# history each time. It stays tracked anyway: the client fetches /plan.json at runtime as
# a static asset, and the build host has no Python or OR-Tools to regenerate it, so
# ignoring it would leave a clean checkout deploying an app with no data in it. Repo size
# is the cheaper problem. Regenerate and sync with:
#     python scripts/run_pipeline.py --days 7 --tasks 600 --monthly --validate
#     cd web && npm run sync

# Downloaded source datasets. Large (16 MB CSV, 82 MB JSON), and their licences differ
# from this repository's, so they are fetched rather than vendored:
#   data.gov.in "Train details"  -> Government Open Data Licence - India
#   Kaggle indian-railways       -> per that dataset's own terms
# The timetable extracted from them is # data/timetable_danapur.imported.csv is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is a 40 KB derived extract -- 543 services over one division, reduced to the ten
# columns this model needs -- not a copy of any source book. Committing it is what makes
# a clone plan against published times rather than the approximate ones, which is the
# difference between demonstrating the idea and demonstrating the system. Its own header
# carries the attribution and the regenerate-rather-than-copy note.
#
# The datasets it derives from stay out: they are 116 MB and their licences are not this
# repository's to grant., also ignored.
